    "result_text": "All 281 tests pass, including the new `Cp16Tests`. \n\nThe change is implemented following the existing computed-field pattern (`membershipNumber`, `customerCode`, `membershipTier`):\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `namesakeCount` integer field to the `Owner` schema (the `OwnerDto` regenerates from this).\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `namesake_count` column field with getter/setter; MapStruct auto-maps it to the DTO by name.\n- **Schema SQL** (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres) \u2014 added the `namesake_count` column so the value persists and is read back by `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n- **`AssignNamesakeCount.java`** \u2014 new pipeline function that counts existing owners sharing the exact same last name. Since the new owner isn't saved yet, `findAll()` correctly excludes it, so the count is the number of *other* owners.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the step in after `assignMembershipTier`, before `save`, under the same transaction governance.\n\nThe first owner with a fresh surname gets `namesakeCount = 0`; a second with the same surname gets `1`, matching the spec.",
